% c271: 253 Cl 1 G4 and Cl 2 E4 on the reprise's downbeat: the retransition's V7 ends with Cl 1 holding the seventh A4 over Cl 2's F sharp 4 (251-252), and the line
%   E5-D sharp 5-B4-A4 now reaches its goal G4 in the same instrument and register instead of breaking off (the G4 came only on beat 2, pizzicato, in Vln II).
%   Aldwell-Schachter PDF 337 Ex. 20-18 (the seventh of V7 in a figurated line resolves down by step; the reading in which it does not is the incorrect one),
%   PDF 332 (a stepwise goal tone the line depends on); as c163 at 20/28 and c092 at 105/305. pp, a level under the p that ends 252 (resolution softer than the dissonance).
