%   second idea's last statement, Cl 1-2, Hn 2 and violas, pp (was sub. p), a level under Fl 1/Ob 1's sub. p tune, as Hn 3 has been since c208.
%   Here the tune is in woodwinds and the fill in woodwind, horn and viola in the oboe's octave (Cl 1 G#4-B4 crosses Ob 1 at 277-278), the close
%   timbres for which the basis must be the weaker; at 121 the tune is in the violins and c308's reason to keep sub. p there still holds.
%   Bass (Bsn 2, Vc) stays sub. p. 281: Cl 1-2 and Hn 2 restate p where they take up the tune's notes with Ob 1, then crescendo with it to f at 285.
