% c041: 269-270 the reprise's call is Bsn 1 solo, p staccato on E3-G3 (was Ob 1, the exposition's colour at 29): the bassoon's humorous staccato
%   (Adler I PDF 226; Ex. VII-95 Dukas, VII-96 Bartok 'Allegretto scherzando'), in its 'sweet, expressive' register (Ex. VII-89); C.a. holds the B and the
%   clarinets drop to pp so the accompanied bassoon is not swallowed (PDF 226: mark the accompaniment's dynamics).
