% c164: 277-280 the double basses rest under the sub. p second idea and enter arco with the contrabassoon at 281 (as 121-125; Adler I PDF 130-131, 139).
% c384 (Rimsky-Korsakov appendix PDF 505-507: the bass always has its octave; ch. IV PDF 125: outer parts not set wide apart without the octaves between filled):
%   253-268 the basses divide in octaves (E1+E2 etc.), unis. at 271. Since c359 the cellos play the countermelody (G3-E4) instead of the pizz. bass E2 of 13-28,
%   so the bass was one pizzicato line in octave 1 with nothing up to G3 (27-33 semitones at 253-266); the divided basses restore 13-28's octave without taking the cellos off c359's line.
dACb = { <e,, e,>4\p^\markup \italic "div." r4 r4 | <e,, e,>4 r4 r4 | <e,, e,>4 r4 r4 | <b,, b,>4 r4 r4 | <e,, e,>4 r4 r4 | <a,, a,>4 r4 r4 | <b,, b,>4 r4 r4 | <e,, e,>4 r4 r4 | <a,, a,>4 r4 r4 | <gis,, gis,>4 r4 r4 | <a,, a,>4 r4 r4 | <b,, b,>4 r4 r4 | <e,, e,>4 r4 r4 | <g,, g,>4 r4 <a,, a,>4 | <b,, b,>4 r4 r4 | <e,, e,>4 r4 r4 | R2. | R2. | e,,4\p\<^\markup \italic "unis." r4 r4 | b,,4 r4 r4 | d,4\f r4 r4 | d,4 r4 r4 | d,4 r4 r4 | R2. | R2.*4 | a,,2\p\<^\markup \italic "arco"( c,4~ | c,4 b,,2) | g,,2( b,,4~ | b,,4 ais,,2) | b,,2.\f~ | b,,2. | e,,2. | e,,4-. r4 r4 | }
