% c383 (A&S Unit 32, PDF 596, 608 sec. 12-13; Dvorak 9/iii 435-485): the reprise's second idea opens in E major (277-280: G sharp for G; 280 is V6/5 of iv,
%   the D natural quaver its seventh, G sharp 2 its leading tone in the bass only, inner voices on E4/B4) and turns minor through iv at 281 (C natural) and i at 283
%   (Cl 1 G4), so the reprise is no longer an unrelieved run of minor keys and G minor at 289 is reached in stages (E major -> E minor -> G minor), as A&S PDF 608 advise
%   for a double-mixture key. Reminder naturals on the first G of each part after its G sharp (283-285). 121-132 stay in E minor, so the idea now has three colours: G major (45), E minor (121), E major turning minor (277).
% c392 (A&S Unit 17 PDF 267; Unit 5 PDF 83): 280 Hn 2/Vla F#4-G#4-E4 (were F#4-E4 on beat 2): no parallel 5ths with the tune's C#6-B5 (Fl 1) and C#5-B4 (Ob 1),
%   which c383's E4 had brought back after c112 removed them (124 F#4-G4). G#4 only on beat 2 (plain I6); E4 on beat 3, so the G sharp is single (bass) when the D natural makes 280 V6/5 of iv, as c383 wants.
% c523: bar 283, the same i6 neighbour as 127 (sC.ily): Cb, Bsn 2, Cbsn G-B instead of E-F#.
